ctuel et propose une stratégie de division","de":"Split-pr ist ein Kommandozeilentool, das den aktuellen Änderungssatz analysiert und eine Aufteilungsstrategie vorschlägt","pt":"O que é split-pr? É uma ferramenta que divide alterações em pedidos de revisão menores e mais gerenciáveis","ru":"Что такое split-pr? Это инструмент, который разделяет изменения на меньшие запросы на проверку","ar":"ما هو Split-PR؟ إنه أداة تقسم التغييرات إلى طلبات مراجعة أصغر وأكثر إدارة"},"features":{"en":["Analyzes current Git diffs using `git diff main...HEAD --stat`","Lists all changed files with `git diff main...HEAD --name-only`","Shows commit history for context","Proposes a splitting strategy for reviewable pull requests","Helps keep changes atomic and reviewable","Integrates with Git workflow for easy deployment"],"zh":["支持Git diff命令","提供详细的文件统计信息","可以列出所有更改的文件","支持显示提交历史","可以将大型更改集分解为逻辑的拉取请求"],"ja":["Git diffコマンドをサポート","詳細なファイル統計情報を提供","すべての変更されたファイルをリストできます","コミット履歴の表示をサポート","大きな変更セットを論理的プルリクエストに分割できます"],"ko":["Git diff 명령어 지원","상세한 파일 통계 정보 제공","모든 변경된 파일을 나열할 수 있습니다","커밋 기록 표시 지원","대형 변경 세트를 논리적인 풀 요청으로 분할할 수 있습니다"],"es":["Análisis del conjunto de cambios actuales con git diff","Propuesta de estrategia de división para cambios atómicos y revisables","Lista de archivos modificados con git diff --name-only","Historial de commits con git log"],"fr":["Analyse de l''ensemble de modifications actuel avec git diff","Proposition d''une stratégie de division pour des modifications atomiques et révisables","Liste des fichiers modifiés avec git diff --name-only","Historique des commits avec git log"],"de":["Analyse des aktuellen Änderungssatzes mit git diff","Vorschlag einer Aufteilungsstrategie für atomare und überprüfbare Änderungen","Liste der geänderten Dateien mit git diff --name-only","Commit-Historie mit git log"],"pt":["Análise de alterações com git diff","Divisão de alterações em pedidos de revisão menores","Melhoria da colaboração e qualidade do código","Integração com CLI para execução de comandos","Análise de commit history para entender as alterações"],"ru":["Анализ изменений с помощью git diff","Разделение изменений на меньшие запросы на проверку","Повышение сотрудничества и качества кода","Интеграция с CLI для выполнения команд","Анализ истории коммитов для понимания изменений"],"ar":["تحليل التغييرات باستخدام git diff","تقسيم التغييرات إلى طلبات مراجعة أصغر","تحسين التعاون وجودة الكود","تكامل مع CLI لتشغيل الأوامر","تحليل تاريخ التعديلات لفهم التغييرات"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use split-pr","what is split-pr","split-pr alternative","split-pr vs GitFlow","split-pr install","split-pr setup guide","Git workflow optimization","reviewable pull requests","large changeset management"],"zh":["Split-PR工具","AI工具","代码审查","Git diff","拉取请求","代码合并","开发工具","版本控制"],"ja":["Split-PRツール","AIエージェント","コードレビュー","Git diff","プルリクエスト","コードマージ","開発ツール","バージョン管理"],"ko":["Split-PR 도구","AI 도구","코드 리뷰","Git diff","풀 요청","코드 병합","개발 도구","버전 관리"],"es":["split-pr","herramientas de línea de comandos","git diff","git log","solicitudes de extracción","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["split-pr","outils en ligne de commande","git diff","git log","demandes d''extraction","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["split-pr","Kommandozeilentools","git diff","git log","Pull-Requests","Softwareentwicklung","Softwareingenieurwesen"],"pt":["split-pr","divisão de alterações","pedidos de revisão","colaboração","qualidade do código","git diff","CLI","análise de commit history"],"ru":["split-pr","разделение изменений","запросы на проверку","сотрудничество","качество кода","git diff","CLI","анализ истории коммитов","ИИ Агенты"],"ar":["Split-PR","تقسيم التغييرات","طلبات مراجعة","التعاون","جودة الكود","git diff","CLI","تحليل تاريخ التعديلات","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"stacklok","repo":"toolhive","repoPath":"stacklok/toolhive","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.291Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"split-pr","description":"Analyzes current changes and suggests how to split them into smaller, reviewable PRs","bodyPreview":"# Split Large PR into Smaller Changes\n\n## Purpose\n\nHelp developers break down large changesets into logical, reviewable pull requests. This skill analyzes the current diff and proposes a splitting strategy that keeps changes atomic and reviewable.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Analyze Current Changes\n\nRun these commands to understand the scope:\n\n```bash\n# Get detailed file statistics\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat\n\n# List all changed files\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only\n\n# Show commit history for cont","body":"# Split Large PR into Smaller Changes\n\n## Purpose\n\nHelp developers break down large changesets into logical, reviewable pull requests. This skill analyzes the current diff and proposes a splitting strategy that keeps changes atomic and reviewable.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Analyze Current Changes\n\nRun these commands to understand the scope:\n\n```bash\n# Get detailed file statistics\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat\n\n# List all changed files\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only\n\n# Show commit history for context\ngit log main...HEAD --oneline\n\n# Count non-generated files changed\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep -v ''vendor/'' | grep -v ''\\.pb\\.go$'' | grep -v ''zz_generated'' | grep -v ''^docs/'' | wc -l\n\n# Count lines changed (excluding generated code)\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat -- . '':(exclude)vendor/*'' '':(exclude)*.pb.go'' '':(exclude)zz_generated*'' '':(exclude)docs/*'' | tail -1\n```\n\n### 2. Evaluate Size and Complexity\n\nAssess whether the changes exceed recommended limits:\n\n- **Target limits per PR**:\n  - < 10 files changed (excluding tests, generated code, docs)\n  - < 400 lines of code changed (excluding tests, generated code, docs)\n  - Changes represent one logical unit of work\n\nIf changes exceed these limits or mix multiple concerns, proceed to split analysis.\n\n### 3. Identify Logical Groupings\n\nExamine the changed files and identify natural boundaries:\n\n- **By component/package**: Group changes by the package or component they affect\n- **By layer**: Separate model changes, business logic, API changes, CLI changes\n- **By concern**: Separate refactoring from new features, bug fixes from enhancements\n- **By dependency**: Identify which changes depend on others\n\nUse these commands to help:\n\n```bash\n# Group changed files by directory\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep -v ''vendor/'' | grep -v ''\\.pb\\.go$'' | cut -d''/'' -f1-2 | sort | uniq -c\n\n# Show changes by package\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep ''\\.go$'' | grep -v ''_test\\.go$'' | cut -d''/'' -f1-3 | sort | uniq -c\n```\n\n### 4. Propose Split Strategy\n\nCreate a structured plan with multiple PRs:\n\nFor each proposed PR, specify:\n- **PR Name**: Brief description (e.g., \"Add base container interface\")\n- **Purpose**: What this PR accomplishes and why it''s needed\n- **Files included**: List of files that would be in this PR\n- **Estimated size**: Approximate lines changed\n- **Dependencies**: Which other proposed PRs this depends on (if any)\n- **Test coverage**: What tests are included\n- **Order**: Suggest the sequence for creating PRs (e.g., \"Create this first\")\n\n### 5. Recommend Creation Order\n\nDetermine the optimal order for creating PRs:\n\n1. **Foundation PRs first**: New interfaces, base types, shared utilities\n2. **Refactoring PRs second**: Changes that use the new foundation\n3. **Feature PRs last**: New functionality that builds on the foundation\n4. **Independent PRs anytime**: Changes that don''t depend on others\n\n### 6. Present Action Plan\n\nProvide a clear, actionable plan:\n\n```markdown\n## Proposed PR Split\n\n### Summary\nCurrently [X] files changed with [Y] lines modified. Recommend splitting into [N] PRs:\n\n### PR 1: [Name] (Create First)\n**Purpose**: [What and why]\n**Files**:\n- path/to/file1.go\n- path/to/file2.go\n**Size**: ~100 LOC\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Tests**: Includes unit tests for new functionality\n\n### PR 2: [Name] (After PR 1)\n**Purpose**: [What and why]\n**Files**:\n- path/to/file3.go\n**Size**: ~150 LOC\n**Dependencies**: Requires PR 1 (uses new interface)\n**Tests**: Integration tests\n\n[... continue for each PR ...]\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Would you like me to help create PR 1 first?\n2. Should I create a tracking issue for the overall work?\n3. Any changes to this split strategy?\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Splitting Principles\n\n- **Each PR should pass tests independently**: Don''t create PRs that break builds\n- **Prefer multiple small PRs over one large PR**: Easier to review and revert\n- **Keep related changes together**: Don''t artificially split code that changes together\n- **Foundation before features**: Establish abstractions before using them\n- **Use feature flags for incomplete work**: If a feature spans multiple PRs\n\n### Common Split Patterns\n\n1. **Refactoring + Feature**:\n   - PR 1: Extract interface and refactor existing code\n   - PR 2: Add new feature using the interface\n\n2. **Multi-layer Feature**:\n   - PR 1: Add data models and database changes\n   - PR 2: Add business logic layer\n   - PR 3: Add API endpoints\n   - PR 4: Add CLI commands\n\n3. **Package Restructuring**:\n   - PR 1: Create new package structure (empty or minimal)\n   - PR 2: Move code to new structure\n   - PR 3: Update imports and references\n   - PR 4: Clean up old structure\n\n4. **Kubernetes Operator Changes**:\n   - PR 1: Update CRD definitions and generate code\n   - PR 2: Update controller logic\n   - PR 3: Add validation and defaulting\n   - PR 4: Update documentation and examples\n\n### What NOT to Split\n\n- **Atomic refactorings**: Renaming that touches many files but is one logical change\n- **Generated code updates**: Proto, CRD, mock updates should stay together\n- **Dependency updates**: Keep go.mod and vendor changes in one PR\n- **Tightly coupled changes**: Changes that don''t make sense independently\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Adding New CLI Command\n\n**Current state**: 8 files changed, 450 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Add business logic to `pkg/` package (3 files, 200 lines)\n- PR 2: Add CLI command and E2E tests (5 files, 250 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Business logic is independently testable and reusable\n\n### Example 2: Refactoring + Feature\n\n**Current state**: 15 files changed, 800 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Extract common interface (2 files, 100 lines)\n- PR 2: Refactor existing implementations to use interface (6 files, 300 lines)\n- PR 3: Add new implementation with feature (7 files, 400 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Each PR is independently valuable and testable\n\n### Example 3: Operator Enhancement\n\n**Current state**: 12 files changed, 600 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Update CRD with new fields and generate code (4 files, 150 lines, mostly generated)\n- PR 2: Update controller to handle new fields (5 files, 300 lines)\n- PR 3: Add validation webhook (3 files, 150 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Each PR represents a complete vertical slice of functionality\n\n## User Interaction\n\nAfter presenting the split strategy:\n\n1. **Ask for feedback**: \"Does this split make sense for your workflow?\"\n2. **Offer to adjust**: Be flexible based on user''s preferences\n3. **Help with first PR**: \"Would you like me to help create PR 1?\"\n4. **Create tracking**: \"Should I create a GitHub issue to track all PRs?\"\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Be pragmatic**: The goal is reviewable PRs, not arbitrary rules\n- **Consider the team**: Some teams prefer different split strategies\n- **Document dependencies**: Make it clear which PRs block others\n- **Test independently**: Each PR should pass CI/CD checks\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:01:02.605Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing to break down large changesets into reviewable pull requests.","zh":"适用于需要将大型变更集拆分为可审查的拉取请求的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが大きな変更セットをレビュー可能なプルリクエストに分割する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"대형 변경 세트를審查 가능한 プル リクエスト로 분할해야 하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan descomponer grandes conjuntos de cambios en solicitudes de extracción revisables.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code ayant besoin de diviser de grands ensembles de modifications en requêtes d''extraction révisables.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die große Änderungssätze in überprüfbare Pull-Anfragen aufteilen müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que precisam dividir conjuntos de alterações grandes em solicitações de pull revisáveis.","ru":"Идеально для агентов код-ревью, которым необходимо разбивать большие наборы изменений на рассматриваемые запросы на включение.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى تقسيم مجموعات التغييرات الكبيرة إلى طلبات سحب قابلة لمراجعة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to analyze Git diffs and propose splitting strategies, keeping changes atomic and reviewable using Git commands like `git diff` and `git diff --stat`.","zh":"赋予代理分析 Git 差异并提出分割策略的能力，使用 Git 命令如 `git diff` 和 `git diff --stat` 来保持更改的原子性和可审查性。","ja":"エージェントが Git 差分を分析し、分割戦略を提案できるようにし、`git diff` や `git diff --stat` などの Git コマンドを使用して変更を原子的にしてレビュー可能な状態に保つ。","ko":"에이전트가 Git 차이를 분석하고 분할 전략을 제안할 수 있도록 하여 `git diff` 및 `git diff --stat`와 같은 Git 명령을 사용하여 변경 사항을 원자적으로 유지하고審查 가능한 상태로 유지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a analizar diferencias de Git y proponer estrategias de división, manteniendo los cambios atómicos y revisables utilizando comandos de Git como `git diff` y `git diff --stat`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''analyser les différences Git et de proposer des stratégies de division, en gardant les modifications atomiques et révisables en utilisant des commandes Git comme `git diff` et `git diff --stat`.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Git-Diffs zu analysieren und Aufteilungsstrategien vorzuschlagen, wobei die Änderungen atomar und überprüfbar bleiben, indem Git-Befehle wie `git diff` und `git diff --stat` verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a analisar diferenças Git e propor estratégias de divisão, mantendo as alterações atômicas e revisáveis usando comandos Git como `git diff` e `git diff --stat`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью анализировать разницу Git и предлагать стратегии разделения, сохраняя изменения атомарными и рассматриваемыми с помощью команд Git, таких как `git diff` и `git diff --stat`.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من تحليلGit diffs واقتراح استراتيجيات تقسيم، مع الحفاظ على التغييرات الذرية والقابلة لمراجعة باستخدام أوامر Git مثل `git diff` و `git diff --stat`."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating large pull request splitting","Generating reviewable changesets","Debugging complex code changes"],"zh":["自动拆分大型拉取请求","生成可审查的变更集","调试复杂代码更改"],"ja":["大きなプルリクエストの自動分割","レビュー可能な変更セットの生成","複雑なコード変更のデバッグ"],"ko":["대형 プル リクエスト의 자동 분할","審查 가능한 변경 세트 생성","복잡한 코드 변경의 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de la división de grandes solicitudes de extracción","Generación de conjuntos de cambios revisables","Depuración de cambios de código complejos"],"fr":["Automatisation de la division de grandes requêtes d''extraction","Génération d''ensembles de modifications révisables","Débogage de modifications de code complexes"],"de":["Automatisierung der Aufteilung großer Pull-Anfragen","Generierung überprüfbarer Änderungssätze","Fehlerbehebung komplexer Codeänderungen"],"pt":["Automatizar a divisão de solicitações de pull grandes","Gerar conjuntos de alterações revisáveis","Depurar alterações de código complexas"],"ru":["Автоматизация разделения больших запросов на включение","Генерация рассматриваемых наборов изменений","Отладка сложных изменений кода"],"ar":["أتمتة تقسيم طلبات السحب الكبيرة","توليد مجموعات التغييرات القابلة لمراجعة","تصحيح أخطاء التغييرات المعقدة للكود"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git repository access","Limited to Git version control system"],"zh":["需要 Git 仓库访问权限","仅限 Git 版本控制系统"],"ja":["Git リポジトリへのアクセスが必要","Git 版本管理システムのみ"],"ko":["Git 리포지토리 액세스가 필요","Git 버전 관리 시스템만 해당"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio Git","Limitado al sistema de control de versiones Git"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel Git","Limité au système de contrôle de version Git"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Git-Repository","Begrenzt auf das Git-Versionierungssystem"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao repositório Git","Limitado ao sistema de controle de versão Git"],"ru":["Требует доступа к репозиторию Git","Ограничен системой контроля версий Git"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مستودع Git","محدود بنظام التحكم في الإصدار Git"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"2dea7c48dbba05891c4b1e544b55515afd407a7b2b49d39265fbcc1ec1314111","qualityScore":57}');
